            <title>[LU-21310] osc: osc_io_write_start() updates mtime after sync write BRW was sent</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21310</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;For a buffered sync write (O_SYNC/O_DSYNC, or a direct write that falls back to buffered IO), the BRW is built and sent from generic_write_sync() inside vvp_io_write_start(), before the OSC cio_start runs. osc_io_write_start() then sets the OSC m/ctime to the current time again, after the BRW was sent. The client shows a newer mtime than the OST has, and after the lock is cancelled stat returns the OST value, so the mtime goes back.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since commit 4fcbd1af9ec3 ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-3321" title="2.x single thread/process throughput degraded from 1.8" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-3321"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-3321&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; clio: add pages into writeback cache in batch"), osc_page_touch_at() already sets the OSC m/ctime as each page is committed, before any BRW is built, so the update in osc_io_write_start() is redundant.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer (new sanity test_39v):&lt;br/&gt;
set fail_loc=0x80000412 (OBD_FAIL_OSC_DELAY_SETTIME), do a 4KiB O_SYNC write, stat, then cancel_lru_locks osc and stat again. The second mtime is 1s older. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
